        {
          "path": "_m/w/s/q/q/dalongdong-baoan-temple-wp/dalongdong-baoan-templ.jpg",
          "filename": "Mural on the wall of Dalongdong Baoan Temple.jpg",
          "caption": "Dalongdong Baoan Temple (Chinese: 大龍峒保安宮; Pe̍h-ōe-jī: Tōa-lông-pōng Pó-an-kiong) also known as the Taipei Baoan Temple (臺北保安宮) is a Taiwanese folk religion temple built in the Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan. The present temple was originally built by clan members in Tong'an, Xiamen, Fujian, who immigrated to Taipei in the early 19th century and gave the temple the name Po-an (保安; Pó-an) in order to \"protect those of Tong'an\" (保佑同安). The Taipei Confucius Temple is located adjacent to the Baoan Temple.",
          "alt": "Dalongdong Baoan Temple (Chinese: 大龍峒保安宮; Pe̍h-ōe-jī: Tōa-lông-pōng Pó-an-kiong) also known as the Taipei Baoan Temple (臺北保安宮) is a Taiwanese folk religion temple built in the Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan. The present temple was originally built by clan members in Tong'an, Xiamen, Fujian, who immigrated to Taipei in the early 19th century and gave the temple the name Po-an (保安; Pó-an) in order to \"protect those of Tong'an\" (保佑同安). The Taipei Confucius Temple is located adjacent to the Baoan Temple.",
